#: src/js/shared/Request.js:39
#. Shown when our translation system (WPML's own) refused a request. %d: the HTTP status it answered with.
msgid ""
"Our translation system did not accept this request (it answered %d). Wait a "
"minute and try again, and contact WPML support if it keeps happening."
msgstr ""

#: src/js/translationDashboard/pickup-translations/model/DownloadTranslations.js:102
#. Why a downloaded translation is listed as not applied on the WPML translation dashboard: the request to save it was cut off (for example by a server time limit), so WPML does not know whether it was saved.
msgid ""
"The site stopped answering before this translation was confirmed. If it was "
"not saved, the next download takes it again."
msgstr ""

#: src/js/translationDashboard/pickup-translations/model/Process.js:211
#. Why a translation is listed as not applied on the WPML translation dashboard: the translation service has it ready, but the job could not be loaded in the browser, so it was not downloaded this time.
msgid ""
"This translation is ready, but its job could not be loaded, so it was not "
"downloaded. The next download takes it."
msgstr ""